            {
              "id": "CVE-2018-6954",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "systemd: Mishandled symlinks in systemd-tmpfiles allows local users to obtain ownership of arbitrary files"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "systemd-tmpfiles in systemd through 237 mishandles symlinks present in non-terminal path components, which allows local users to obtain ownership of arbitrary files via vectors involving creation of a directory and a file under that directory, and later replacing that directory with a symlink. This occurs even if the fs.protected_symlinks sysctl is turned on."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2018-6954",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.8",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "vulnerability",
                  "low"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2018-7169",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "shadow-utils: newgidmap allows unprivileged user to drop supplementary groups potentially allowing privilege escalation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An issue was discovered in shadow 4.5. newgidmap (in shadow-utils) is setuid and allows an unprivileged user to be placed in a user namespace where setgroups(2) is permitted. This allows an attacker to remove themselves from a supplementary group, which may allow access to certain filesystem paths if the administrator has used \"group blacklisting\" (e.g., chmod g-rwx) to restrict access to paths. This flaw effectively reverts a security feature in the kernel (in particular, the /proc/self/setgroups knob) to prevent this sort of privilege escalation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2018-7169",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.3",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "vulnerability",
                  "low"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2018-9234",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GnuPG: Unenforced configuration allows for apparently valid certifications actually signed by signing subkeys"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GnuPG 2.2.4 and 2.2.5 does not enforce a configuration in which key certification requires an offline master Certify key, which results in apparently valid certifications that occurred only with access to a signing subkey."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2018-9234",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "vulnerability",
                  "low"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2019-11038",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "gd: Information disclosure in gdImageCreateFromXbm()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When using the gdImageCreateFromXbm() function in the GD Graphics Library (aka LibGD) 2.2.5, as used in the PHP GD extension in PHP versions 7.1.x below 7.1.30, 7.2.x below 7.2.19 and 7.3.x below 7.3.6, it is possible to supply data that will cause the function to use the value of uninitialized variable. This may lead to disclosing contents of the stack that has been left there by previous code."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-11038",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.3",
                "tags": [
